Submitting, proposing, committing, uploading, or otherwise providing a change does
not mean that the change is approved, accepted, or incorporated into the Software.
All proposed changes—including commits, pull requests, patches, merge requests,
issue-linked changes, generated files, documentation, assets, and other
modifications—are subject to review and approval by the project’s authorized
maintainers, using the project’s designated contribution process.

Only an authorized maintainer may approve or accept a proposed change on behalf
of the project. Approval may be expressed through the project’s designated review
mechanism or other clear written confirmation. A commit existing in a repository,
a review comment, automated check, or submission alone is not approval unless
the project’s designated process explicitly treats it as such. Maintainers may
request revisions, decline, close, revert, or omit proposed changes at their
discretion, subject to applicable law and the rights granted under this License.

Approval or acceptance of a change does not transfer ownership from its
Contributor. The contribution license grant in this License applies to intentionally
submitted Contributions as stated above, whether or not the project ultimately
accepts or merges them; this approval section governs project inclusion and does
not withdraw or narrow that grant.

